0. SUMMARY (plain words; the numbered clauses below are what counts)
   Using QuadCut is free, and commercial use is allowed: you may run it at work,
   demo it to clients, and use it in commercial projects.
   What is not allowed is selling the software itself - see clause 3.

1. USE
   You may use QuadCut free of charge, for any lawful purpose, personal or
   commercial, on any number of computers that you own or control.
   "Commercial use" means using the software as a tool in the course of
   business - demos, presentations, day-to-day work inside a company, work
   delivered to a client, and so on. Files you manage with QuadCut, and anything
   you produce with it, belong to you and are not restricted by this license.

2. REDISTRIBUTION
   You may redistribute complete, unmodified copies of QuadCut free of charge,
   provided that (a) this license and the complete, unmodified program are
   included, and (b) no fee of any kind is charged for the copy or for its
   distribution - including indirect charges such as paid membership, paid cloud
   storage, paid download traffic or a minimum purchase.

3. NO SALE OF THE SOFTWARE
   You may not sell, resell, rent, lease, sublicense or otherwise monetise
   QuadCut itself. In particular you may not
   (a) sell or charge for copies of QuadCut, or for access to a download of it;
   (b) distribute it together with, or as an inducement to buy, a paid product,
       paid service or paid membership;
   (c) distribute a modified, repackaged, translated, renamed or otherwise
       altered version for money;
   (d) charge others for the act of installing, configuring or delivering
       QuadCut as such.
   This clause restricts the software only. It does not restrict your own work:
   files you manage, documents you produce and demonstrations you give with
   QuadCut may of course be part of your business.

4. RESTRICTIONS
   You may not modify, adapt, translate, decompile, disassemble,
   reverse-engineer or create derivative works from QuadCut. You may not
   redistribute it in any modified form, or as part of another product, without
   the author's prior written permission.

5. NO WARRANTY
   QuadCut is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including but not limited to the implied warranties of
   merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. You
   use it at your own risk.

6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
   In no event shall the author be liable for any claim, damage or other
   liability, whether in an action of contract, tort or otherwise, arising
   from, out of or in connection with QuadCut or its use or other dealings in
   QuadCut.

7. TERMINATION
   Any breach of section 2, 3 or 4 terminates the permissions granted here. On
   termination you must stop using and distributing QuadCut and delete all
   copies in your possession.

